"<div><div class=\" response-message\"></div></div><div><div class=\" response-message\"><h1>Path 1 Exploration</h1>\n<h2>Starting Point</h2>\n<p><strong>Step S0:</strong> Restate the linear equation 3x + 7 = 22 and identify x as the variable to be solved.</p>\n<p>$$3x + 7 = 22$$</p>\n<hr />\n</div></div><div><div class=\" response-message\"><h3>Step S1: algebraic</h3>\n<p>Subtract 7 from both sides of the equation to isolate the term containing x.</p>\n<p>$$3x + 7 - 7 = 22 - 7$$</p>\n<p><em>Justification:</em> Subtraction Property of Equality, which states that if $a = b$, then $a - c = b - c$.</p>\n</div></div><div><div class=\" response-message\"><h3>Step S2: simplification</h3>\n<p>Simplify both sides of the equation by performing the subtraction.</p>\n<p>$$3x = 15$$</p>\n<p><em>Justification:</em> Arithmetic simplification of the terms on both sides of the equation ($7 - 7 = 0$ and $22 - 7 = 15$).</p>\n</div></div><div><div class=\" response-message\"><h3>Step S3: algebraic</h3>\n<p>Divide both sides of the equation by 3 to isolate the variable x.</p>\n<p>$$\\frac{3x}{3} = \\frac{15}{3}$$</p>\n<p><em>Justification:</em> Division Property of Equality, which states that if $a = b$ and $c \\neq 0$, then $\\frac{a}{c} = \\frac{b}{c}$.</p>\n</div></div><div><div class=\" response-message\"><h3>Step S4: simplification</h3>\n<p>Simplify both sides of the equation to find the value of x.</p>\n<p>$$x = 5$$</p>\n<p><em>Justification:</em> Arithmetic simplification of the terms on both sides of the equation (\\frac{3}{3} = 1 and \\frac{15}{3} = 5).</p>\n</div></div><div><div class=\" response-message\"><p>✅ <strong>Goal Reached!</strong></p>\n<p>The goal was to find the value of x for the equation 3x + 7 = 22. The equation has been solved, resulting in x = 5.</p>\n</div></div><div><div class=\" completion-message response-message\"></div></div>"